welcome back everyone to streaming the  galaxy my name is rocket riley and today  we're going to be going over a frame by  frame breakdown of pixar's new trailer  for light year the 3d animated film  featuring chris evans based upon the  real life character in the toy story  universe that the toy buzz lightyear is  based upon but before we get started if  you're new to the channel please hit the  subscribe button and click the bell icon  to be notified when we upload a new  video now let's take a deeper look into  all the clues and easter eggs you may  have missed in the trailer  the trailer starts us off with a status  check from mission control similar to  checks you may have seen in movies like  the martian or from real life rocket  launch sequences as buzz is zipping up  his jacket we also notice that he has o  positive blood while this likely won't  have an impact on the story it's just  nice to see that pixar never misses a  single detail  we also see a crystal-like structure in  a fuel cell inserted into the spaceship  due for launch likely as the main fuel  source for interstellar travel  we see the flight trajectory for the  ship as it launches around the sun using  its gravitational pull to perform a  slingshot maneuver deeper into space  next we see the mission control space  for the journey and the star command  logo is seen in the top left corner in  case you weren't aware star command is  the training and authority association  which manages the galaxy's space rangers  and cadets  this is a nod to the toy buzz's actions  in the first toy story movie as well as  the original disney series buzz received  titled buzz lightyear of star command  which ran for a total of four seasons  we also now know the release date for  the film which is june 17th 2022  the ship has a successful launch into  space and buzz then presses the hyper  launch button and puts on a frontal  shield propelling himself further into  the depths of space as buzz's ship flies  across the bright sun david bowie's  starman begins to play  we then see the base on which buzz will  likely be staying during his space  voyage and it looks quite similar to the  atmosphere of mars but we can see  condensation on the windows so it's more  likely a different planet we also see  buzz in his star command t-shirt another  nod to the original tv show  next we see a ship flying through  several rings in space maybe used as  launch points to a different destination  we see buzz hiding behind a rock along  with a robot who could be xr or  experimental ranger from the tv show who  was the first robot space ranger in star  command history we next see a scene that  looks eerily similar to the scene in  star wars the empire strikes back where  luke crash lands on dagobah the  forgotten swamp covered planet where  yoda trains luke to use the force  we then see what looks like a giant  launch portal on a planet with a  breathable atmosphere since buzz is  outside without a helmet we also see  several star command employees and an  officer who may end up being one of the  story's antagonist  we also see buzz's ship flying through  space sparking as he struggles to make  control of the obviously damaged ship we  see buzz playing with and being scared  by a toy cat while in one of the star  command bases  we see a robot giving a short lesson to  buzz and another ranger and based upon  the drawings on the whiteboard it seems  like the lesson is similar to the one we  learned from interstellar it looks like  due to the high light speed velocity at  which buzz will be traveling it will  seem like just minutes for him on his  journey while for others it will take  years  because of the hyper speed button buzz  pushes in the trailer every minute for  him will be like one year for those on  earth  buzz is then attacked by a green monster  likely similar to some of the monsters  we saw in the star command tv show we  then see the same toy cat attached to  the ship likely performing some sort of  function that assists with navigation  and we can see that the cat has a name  in the subtitles socks  we then catch a glimpse of the hornets  zerg's evil army of yellow robots seen  in the tv show as well  we also see a case opening up which may  contain the evil emperor zerg likely to  be the main antagonist of the movie near  the end of the trailer we finally get to  see buzz's traditional star suit with  the green and white accents along with  the classic wrist laser  the trailer ends with buzz and another  space ranger in their green and white  star suits who say to each other to  infinity and  leaving us all to scream beyond at home  this movie looks like it will provide  the story of a much more realistic space  ranger rather than the fantastical one  we saw in the tv series i'm so excited  to see what this movie brings especially  since chris evans will be voicing the  character of buzz it'll be great to see  movies like this which expand upon the  already established toy story universe  taking a completely new spin on the  action figure  well that's going to be everything from  us today on disney's newest trailer for  light year if you enjoyed the video  please hit the like button and don't  forget to subscribe for more great  content what are your theories about the  new trailer we'd like to know what you  think so drop your thoughts in the  comment section below from everyone here  at stream in the galaxy we hope you have  a great day and thanks for watching  [Music]  you
 

